    <categoryEntry name="Daemonic Summoner" id="c47f-35e6-c08b-7d7d" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="[Action] Summon ritual" id="e531-815e-c995-bd82" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">A unit with the Daemonic Summoner Keyword can do this action at the beggining of the Command phase, and it ends at the end of the Movement phase, before the Reinforcements step.
Roll 3D6, if you roll any double roll result, the unit making this action suffers 1 mortal wound. If you roll three rolls of the same result, the unit making this action suffers 1D3 mortal wounds.
Then, you can select, from the Chaos - Daemons library, up to two units without CHARACTER Keyword, without any upgrade, with a PL cost equal or lesser than half the result (rounding up), and set it up on the battlefield D3+6&quot; away from enemy models, as reinforcements.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </categoryEntry>
  </categoryEntries>
