      <profiles>
        <profile name="Daemonic Summoning Ritual" id="71dd-be1e-380f-d760" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">If every unit of your Detachment has the CHAOS DAEMONS Keyword, at the start of each Command phase, you can make a Summoning Ritual.
To do so, roll 2D6, and you can select any number of units without CHARACTER Keyword that either has returned to the Warp or had been destroyed, as Reinforcements, with a combined PL cost equal or lesser than the result.

Add an additional D6 to the roll if your WARLORD is a GREATER DAEMON model and is on the Battlefield.

The number of times you can make a Summoning Ritual depends of the size of battle you are playing, as shown below:</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="  Warp Storm Effects" id="3ddb-2e95-ef8b-605c" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">If every unit of your Detachment has the FACTION: CHAOS DAEMONS Keyword, at the start of each battle round, you can make a Warp Storm roll. 
To do so, roll up to nine D6. For each 4+, gain 1 Warp Storm point (WSP).
 - If your Warlord have the Mark of Nurgle, you can roll up to 7 D6.
 - If your Warlord have the Mark of Khorne, you can roll up to 8 D6.
 - If your Warlord have the Mark of Slaanesh, you can roll up to 6 D6, and can re-roll any of the dice.
WSP can be spent during that battle round on the Warp Storm effects.
You can always select effects from UNDIVIDED, and, if your Warlord has a dedicated Chaos Mark, you can also select Warp Storm effects from that Chaos allegiance.
Unless stated otherwise, any unspent WSP are lost at the beginning of the next Battle Round.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
